## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond `web/package-lock.json`; a differing leaf beyond the three `fast-uri` fields; `fast-uri` reachable from a prod root; a dependent range 3.1.9 fails; a `resolved` host other than `registry.npmjs.org` or an `integrity` that does not match the registry; any of the four advisories still reported at head; a new advisory at head that base lacks; a failed check-run (other than CodeQL `neutral` as read); an open CodeQL alert on the PR ref; a secret; a non-Dependabot commit; the head moved. *Major:* a claim contradicted by measurement that changes the verdict's basis (for example the four ids absent at main already: then the bump fixes nothing the registry still reports, say so); `npm ls` and the JSON deep-compare disagreeing; a worse suite at head. *Minor/Note:* the repo's audit step cannot show the fix (high/critical only; a threshold fact for HPSMPOC-346, not a PR defect); an unverified Dependabot signature; a feed lag between two audit reads; ajv being the only dependent. **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6 clean and measured. The PR exists, so CI is evidence; GO WITH FINDINGS if only Notes; NO GO on any Blocker; a NO GO is a one-line fix-shape in prose (for a Dependabot PR: close and let it re-open, or a human lockfile PR; Tuesday decides). Round 1 of 2. **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B597: #209 PENDING`; verdict form):** `GATE VERDICT B597: #209 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 4dabf18 (round 1 of 2 - delta <1 path, 1 commit, +3 -3; lockfile leaves differing 3 y/n; package.json equal y/n; non-ASCII 0 y/n> - graph <dependents n; all ranges satisfied y/n; dev-only y/n> - audit <ids at main n of 4; ids at head n of 4; repo dev-audit rc main n head n; prod audit rc main n head n; new advisories at head n> - suites <relied on PR jobs | head: web n passed n failed, lint rc n, typecheck rc n> - checks <n completed success of 16; CodeQL neutral read as: <short>; open alerts n> - provenance <author dependabot y/n; commits 1 y/n; head unmoved y/n; main sha7 at start and end> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-6 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B597-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the audit table (id, severity, range, first patched, at main, at head), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether the head-pinned squash can go now; what HPSMPOC-346 still owes: the repo's audit gate does not see moderate advisories), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B597 #209 dependabot/npm_and_yarn/web/fast-uri-3.1.9 @ 4dabf18 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 1 of 2; CI <complete|pending: names|red: names>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict), with the findings ids and severities in the line above it (`B597-1 Minor`), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

